[Title "Philidor's Legacy"]
[Goal "White to play and force mate"]
[Themes "smothered mate, double check, queen sacrifice"]
[Rating "1500"]
[Source "Classic study, after Philidor"]
[FEN "5rk1/5Npp/8/8/8/1Q6/6PP/6K1 w - - 0 1"]

1. Nh6+ {Double check. The knight hits g8 and the queen's diagonal to g8 opens
behind it, so no capture and no block will do — the king has to move.} Kh8
{Forced: f7 and g8 are both covered by the queen, and f8 is the rook's own square.}
2. Qg8+ {The point. The queen is given away to force the rook onto g8, where it
takes the last flight square away from its own king.}
(2. Nf7+ Kg8 3. Nh6+ Kh8 {A draw by repetition. The knight can check forever,
but checks that repeat are not progress.}) 2... Rxg8
{Forced — the king cannot take on g8 because the knight on h6 defends it.}
3. Nf7# {Smothered: the king's own rook and pawns do the work of the mating net.}
